ng/</guid><description>&lt;aside class="source-note" aria-label="Text provenance"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Original text&lt;/strong&gt;
 &lt;span&gt; · English&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/aside&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When I was playing on the cave levels of &lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SiNiSistar2&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt; (v1.2.1), I noticed a unique lighting behavior—no matter which direction the light is from, the highlights were &amp;quot;locked&amp;quot; on the &lt;strong&gt;left&lt;/strong&gt; edges of the stones.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;They were clearly illuminated by her light when positioned to the right of Lelia; however, once Lelia passes them, they receded into darkness while still shimmering exclusively on their &lt;strong&gt;left&lt;/strong&gt; edges. To figure out what caused that, I viewed the textures in Unity.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>About</title><link>https://akiloneus.github.io/about/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://akiloneus.github.io/about/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Greetings, this is Akiloneus. I am really into games and trying to make my own.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Welcome to Kessaria—my personal blog. I plan to add more posts and projects here, to keep a record of them and share what I have built.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thank you for visiting.&lt;/p&gt;
